   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the urban development corporation act, in relation to allowing\nbusinesses to use funds received from the minority and women-owned business\ndevelopment and lending program for the purpose of refinancing existing debt",
    "basePrintNo": "S1356",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1356-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §16-c, UDC Act (as proposed in S.571 & A.6420)",
    "lawSection": "New York State Urban Development Corporation Act",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1356\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the urban development corporation act, in relation  to\nallowing  businesses  to  use  funds  received  from  the minority and\nwomen-owned business development and lending program for  the  purpose\nof refinancing existing debt\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes technical changes to provisions\nof L.2022, c.568, to clarify that the refinancing provisions of the\nunderlying bill apply to commercial and business loans.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter to specify that refinanc-\ning provisions apply to commercial and business loans only.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 568 of the Laws of 2022. S.571 and A..6420\nboth passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in May 2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2022 amending the urban development corporation\nact relating to allowing businesses to use funds received from the\nminority and women-owned business development and lending program for\nthe purpose of refinancing existing debt, as proposed in legislative\nbills numbers S.571 and A. 6420, takes effect.\n",
